Subject: [PATCH] build: upgrade gRPC, Thrift, x/image, and x/crypto past known advisories

SeaweedFS 4.40 pins gRPC 1.81.1 (GHSA-hrxh-6v49-42gf and, below 1.83.1,
GHSA-vp52-pcj8-j9qc), golang.org/x/image 0.43.0 (GO-2026-6222),
golang.org/x/crypto 0.54.0 (GO-2026-6303, GO-2026-6354, and
GO-2026-6355, reachable through weed/sftpd), and Apache Thrift at a
pre-0.23.1 commit that is affected by GHSA-8wv5-x4w7-5gww. Thrift moves
to the 0.24.0 release, which also carries the 32-bit range fix that the
upstream replace directive pinned, so the replace is dropped as upstream
master did. Upgrading x/image also lifts golang.org/x/mod, net, text,
and tools to the versions its module graph requires; gRPC 1.83.1 lifts
its OpenTelemetry, genproto, cel, and spiffe dependencies. x/crypto
0.56.0 requires Go 1.26, so the go directive moves from 1.25.8 to
1.26.0 and the Eneo builder image tracks Go 1.26. Keep this downstream
patch until an upstream SeaweedFS release includes gRPC 1.83.1, Thrift
0.24.0, x/image 0.45.0, and x/crypto 0.56.0 or newer.

